project code, including commercial use.

Third-party services and data
-----------------------------

The WTFPL applies to the project code. It does NOT grant rights to data,
trademarks, content or services provided by third parties and accessed by the
firmware at runtime.

SmallTV Deutsch/VVO can access, among others:

- Verkehrsverbund Oberelbe (VVO)
- Open-Meteo
- adsb.lol
- adsbdb
- optionally aviationstack
- OpenStreetMap map tiles in the web interface

Those services and data remain subject to their respective terms of use,
licences, rate limits and attribution requirements. Some free services used by
the default configuration are intended only for private/non-commercial use or
otherwise restrict reuse of their data.

Commercial use of the project code is therefore not the same as permission to
commercially use every configured external data source. Anyone using,
distributing or integrating this firmware commercially is responsible for
obtaining suitable rights for the external services they actually use, or for
replacing them with appropriately licensed alternatives.

This project notice does not modify the WTFPL. It only clarifies that the
project cannot license rights belonging to third parties.
